1.Create an HTML file that uses semantic tags to build a simple blog post layout with <header> for the blog title, <nav> for navigation links (Home, Explore, About), 
<article> for the main post content, and <footer> for copyright information.
Ans.
<html>
<head>
    <title>My Simple Blog</title>
</head>
<body>
    <header>
        <h1>Developer Insights</h1>
        <p>A blog about web development, design, and coding best practices.</p>
    </header>

    <nav>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="#home">Home</a></li>
            <li><a href="#explore">Explore</a></li>
            <li><a href="#about">About</a></li>
        </ul>
    </nav>

    <main>
        <article>
            <h2>Getting Started with Semantic HTML5</h2>
            <p>Published on <time datetime="2026-10-23">October 23, 2026</time> by <strong>Jane Doe</strong></p>
            <p>Semantic HTML elements clearly describe their meaning to both the browser and the developer. Tags like <code>&lt;article&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;header&gt;</code>, and <code>&lt;footer&gt;</code> empower screen readers and search engines to interpret page hierarchy accurately.</p>
        </article>
    </main>

    <footer>
        <p>&copy; 2026 Developer Insights. All rights reserved.</p>
    </footer>

</body>
</html>


